# Keep shell scripts LF whatever the host's `core.autocrlf` says.
#
# Windows checkouts default to `core.autocrlf=true`, which rewrites every text
# file to CRLF -- including the bash entry points under `scripts/`. A CRLF bash
# script fails on its first line with `set: pipefail: invalid option name`, and
# `scripts/e2e-wsl.sh` sources `e2e-wsl-setup.sh`, so the whole E2E suite was
# unrunnable from WSL while looking like a Docker or Playwright problem.
*.sh text eol=lf
